// --- Light ---
//
// One lamp at the mouth of each cross recess, one up in the roof to bring the
// ribs out of the dark, the pair the well needs, and a close pair grazing the
// broad faces of the monolith so the slab keeps an edge instead of going flat
// against the dark behind it. Nothing here is baked with shadows, so every
// radius is kept short enough to die before it reaches the next room.
//
// The pair under the well is kept tight on purpose: at 20 m it dies well short
// of the walls, so what it lights is the ribs around the mouth and the top of
// the slab, and the floor stays as dark as the rest of the room.
//
// The pair has to sit outside the slab: a lamp buried in it would face the
// backs of its own faces and light nothing.

